{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Vanishing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Vanishing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.RemovableSingularity","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Liouville","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.eq_zero_of_symm_growth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.eq_zero_of_symm_growth","kind":"theorem","line":9,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Vanishing.lean#L9-L149","doc":"**Proposition D3b (vanishing, pure complex analysis).** A function holomorphic on `ℂ ∖ {0,1}`,\nsymmetric under `z ↦ 1 - z`, with `F(1/z)·z = -F(z)`, and with `|F(z)| ≤ C/√|z|` near `0`,\nvanishes. The growth bound removes the singularity at `0`, the symmetry removes the one at `1`,\nthe inversion law gives linear growth at `∞`, and Liouville finishes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}